# One rule, two reasons.
#
# `dsh-smith`'s push tooling uploads blob bytes obtained from `git cat-file blob`,
# and a CRLF conversion in the working tree makes the checked-out file differ from
# the blob it should be. Pinning the repository to LF keeps the stored bytes and
# the working tree in agreement on every platform, so a fresh clone is clean
# rather than showing every tracked file as modified.
#
# The second reason is specific to this package: its sources carry Chinese prose
# in comments, doc blocks and tool descriptions, and the README is written in
# Chinese. A toolchain that rewrote line endings through a locale-dependent code
# page would corrupt that text, so the pin matters more here than it does for an
# ASCII-only package.
* text=auto eol=lf
